            <ArticleTitle>Transesophageal echocardiographic (TEE) evaluation of intracardiac and pericardial masses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>849-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Transesophageal echocardiography has assisted the detection of intracardiac masses and, in certain cases, aided our ability to define the specific type of mass. This technique, when coupled with three-dimensional imaging, may help to define infiltration of the wall. TEE aids in the intraoperative management of cardiac tumors.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
